Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline follows an Institute-of-Medicine-palliative-care-definition.
Every palliative-care provides a pain-and-other-symptom-relief.
Every palliative-care supports a patient-quality-of-life.
Every palliative-care focuses on a serious-advanced-illness-patient-group.
If a patient has a serious-advanced-illness and receives a care that provides a pain-and-other-symptom-relief and that supports a patient-quality-of-life then the patient receives a palliative-care.
